joshk was getting annoyed in his home. He came from a big family - he
was the youngest in a family with 11 children, oddly, all named joshk as
well. The rest had all grown up and taken their various professions -
valkyries, samurai, wizards, what have you. joshk felt alone as his
brothers obtained their riches and favor with their gods. Unfortunately,
he stepped down the wrong path and became a common thief, until he
decided to embark on his own adventure so he could be just like his
brothers.

He had virtually nothing except the clothes on his back - and that
wasn't much either. A +1 leather armor was Death's only obstacle to
joshk. joshk heard from his brothers that drinking fountains was very
profitable early on, so he started drinking. Suddenly, a hideous water
demon appeared, and he was none too happy. So he escaped, rushing down
floor after floor in mortal fear, dispatching foes with his +0 daggers
from a distance. Reaching a coaligned altar below the Oracle,
Stormbringer ensued after some generosity towards Kos, and he was very
careful to keep it sheathed when around priests and people who could
easily do him in if angered.

Early on, he found the remains of a slain Valkyrie - fortunately, not
one of his sisters. He rummaged through her inventory and found a very
helpful +3 small shield and some gold and food.

joshk rampaged through the Gnomish Mines and reached Bustling Town. It
was here that he found a cloak of protection which served him well for a
long time. Unfortunately, he forgot to keep Stormbringer sheathed down
here, and accidentally hit a watch captain and the cross-aligned priest
in the temple. Hot on his feet he sped away, but managed to kill all of
the watchmen with the help of some divine intervention from Kos when his
HP dropped very low. He left the priest alone. Those chaps have really
foul temper tantrums, and joshk didn't want to risk the wrath of the
temple's god because he lacked both magic resistance and reflection.

His luck improved some more as he received two throne genocides, but he
turned them down; joshk was a purist, and would only kill monsters by
his own blade. Then, perhaps as recompensation for his choices, a throne
offered him a wish. He got a blessed greased +2 silver dragon scale mail
- a very nice fit. Yet another throne granted him another wish: this
time, a blessed greased fixed +2 pair of speed boots, which he was
content to receive at +0.

Intending to try for crowning at a very early stage, joshk went back up
to the Sokoban altar and sacrificed some more monsters thanks to a wand
of create monster. He received a spellbook of dig and the next time he
sacrificed, he received Giantslayer! What a piece of junk, he thought,
and flung it into the pile of lousy armor and corpses. Unfortunately, he
forgot about the fact that he had just received the sword and tested
Kos' patience again, only to discover that he was no longer very happy.
Searching frantically for a means to mollify Kos, joshk went up a floor
and murdered the Oracle, hoping that her corpse would prove his devotion
to Kos. Using his ring of teleport control that he found in the mines,
he was able to dig down from the Oracle level and quickly teleport
straight to the altar. But to his surprise, Yeenoghu appeared; joshk
pissed his pants, and warily led him to Sokoban and left him there for
good. And Kos was still angry.

Later, he located a giant mimic; again, he levelported to the Sokoban
altar and sacrificed it. Kos finally was mollified, and joshk breathed a
sigh of relief.

Medusa was a piece of cake thanks to his reflection. joshk tapped her on
the shoulder, and she opened her eyes and turned to stone from her own
reflection. He then went to the Castle and kicked everyone's butt: the
wand of wishing yielded +2 gauntlets of dexterity, a +2 T-shirt, two
magic markers, and 2 blessed scrolls of charging. He picked up a silver
saber off a captain's corpse and started training with it until he got
skilled.

The Quest was a cakewalk after obtaining protection from a cross-aligned
priest in the dungeon and enchanting armor to +4 or +5, and weapons to
+6 (Stormbringer) and +7 (ag saber) respectively. Three tries were
required to get to the Master Assassin, and joshk let him feel the sting
of Stormbringer and he was soon dead. After running back up he was
pleased to know that the Master Of Thieves would be letting him keep the
Master Key Of Thievery that he reclaimed from MA.

Hell was easy too. Gehennom yielded another magic marker which he used
to re-enchant his weapons which got disenchanted by a disenchanter. Both
were +6 now. After digging like crazy, he finally found the vibrating
square, marked it with gold, and ran back up to slay the Wizard of
Yendor. Rodney was easy; joshk showed him the business end of a wand of
death. He picked up the book, performed the invocation, sliced through
the priests and undead like hot butter, also introduced the high priest
of Moloch to his wand of death, and picked up the Amulet.

The ascension run was easy; two interventions from Rodney in total, and
only a few occurences of the Force. He escaped the dungeon and appeared
on the plane of Earth, where he decided to find the portal to the plane
of air without the help of a scroll of gold detection (since he only had
3 in total.) Mercifully, an earth elemental of all creatures left one,
and he found the portal after 'practicing' his forgotten spell of Dig.
He plowed through the xorns and elementals and appeared on the plane of
Air, which he cleaned out as well, including one Archon. The plane of
Fire resulted in two Archons, both of which were easily dispatched while
blind.

The plane of water was easy; searching of all things revealed the magic
portal fairly quickly, so after killing some elementals and sea
creatures he jumped in before it fell out of sight.

Astral was simple, although joshk accidentally hit some coaligned
priests a few times while in the fever of battle - easily fixed with
taming. To his surprise, a Barbarian was waiting for him at the door to
an altar - wielding the Vorpal Blade. Before joshk knew it, he
discovered what it was like to exist with his head not attached to his
body, but only for a split second - his amulet of life saving revived
him, and he quickly destroyed Kevin the Raider and picked up Vorpal
Blade. The rest of the hostiles were easily killed with wands of death
and double doses of Stormbringer.

After draining Pestilence and Famine to very low levels, joshk wrote
some scrolls of taming and tried to tame both demons. Unfortunately,
only Pestilence was tamed before his magic marker ran completely dry, so
he ran to the altar and offered the Amulet to Kos - with Pestilence, of
course, and a soldier ant he accidentally tamed while trying to tame the
two riders. joshk named him Goober right before he offered the Amulet,
but unfortunately he was unable to come along for the ride because he
was busy eating.

joshk placed the Amulet on the altar and all of his siblings suddenly
came to greet him from the sky. So that's where they had been all this
time! Kos offered him Immortality which he gratefully accepted, and
joshk went off to party and get drunk with all of his brothers and
sisters.

